-- title:
--   Formal descent data give q-expansions of the Hecke coset polynomial
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $\ell$ assumed prime, a unit $\zeta$ of `CyclotomicField ℓ ℚ` together with a proof `hζ` that $\zeta$ is a primitive $\ell$-th root of unity, and a family $c : \mathbb{N} \to$ `LaurentSeries ℚ` of rational Laurent series. Assume [`ModularCurve.PhiGen.PhiGenDescends ℓ ζ c`](def/ModularCurve_PhiGen.html#L302), i.e. for every $k$ the $k$-th coefficient of the polynomial $\prod_{i : \mathrm{Fin}(\ell+1)} (X - C(\mathrm{conj}\,\ell\,\zeta\,i))$ over Laurent series with coefficients in the cyclotomic field equals the image under `coeffEmb` of `qExpand ℚ ℓ (c k)`, the series obtained from $c_k$ by multiplying all exponents by $\ell$; here $\mathrm{conj}\,\ell\,\zeta\,i$ is `cosetSubst ζ (cosetA ℓ i) (cosetB ℓ i)` applied to the coefficientwise image of the Laurent series [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), the formal stand-ins for the $\ell+1$ Hecke conjugates of $j$. Then for every $k : \mathbb{N}$ and every $\tau$ in the upper half-plane, the family indexed by $m \in \mathbb{Z}$ whose $m$-th term is the rational number $\mathrm{coeff}_m(c_k)$, viewed in $\mathbb{C}$, times $q^m$ with $q =$ `Function.Periodic.qParam 1 τ` $= e^{2\pi i \tau}$, is summable with sum the $k$-th coefficient of the polynomial
--   $$\bigl(X - C\,\tilde j(\beta_\infty \tau)\bigr)\prod_{b : \mathrm{Fin}\,\ell}\bigl(X - C\,\tilde j(\beta_b \tau)\bigr) \in \mathbb{C}[X],$$
--   where $\tilde j = E_4^3/\Delta$ in the normalisation `ModularForm.E₄` and `ModularForm.discriminant`, $\beta_\infty =$ `heckeDiagMatrix ℓ` $= \begin{pmatrix}\ell&0\\0&1\end{pmatrix}$ and $\beta_b =$ `heckeMatrix ℓ b` $= \begin{pmatrix}1&b\\0&\ell\end{pmatrix}$ act on the upper half-plane through $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$.
--
--   This is the analytic–formal bridge for the modular polynomial of level $\ell$: it identifies a formal solution of the descent equations for the Hecke coset product with the $q$-expansion, convergent on the upper half-plane, of the corresponding elementary symmetric function of the values $\tilde j(\beta_i\tau)$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.PhiGen.mem_adjoin_jq_of_phiGenDescends`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PhiGen.mem_adjoin_jq_of_phiGenDescends) to place these symmetric functions in the algebra generated by $j$.
